  "TITLE": "Carrying Capacity:<br>Why Growth Bends",
  "LEAD": "Every population starts out nearly exponential, but each new individual leaves less food, space and light for the rest, so growth slows and levels off at the environment&rsquo;s carrying capacity, K. The result is an S-curve whose steepest point sits at exactly half of K. A chemical reaction that feeds its own catalyst follows the same curve: it accelerates while there is plenty of reactant, then stalls as the reactant runs out.",
